<div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><section class="snap"><h2>Richmond at a glance</h2>
<dl class="snap-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Madison County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>The Bluegrass</dd></div><div><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Historic homes in the downtown area, a large stock of student rentals and apartments near the university, growing subdivisions and farm properties stretching to the Kentucky River.</dd></div></dl>
<h3>Local claim risks</h3><ul class="tags"><li>Hail</li><li>Straight-line wind</li><li>Ice storms</li><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Water damage in rentals</li></ul>
<h3>Neighborhoods and nearby communities</h3><ul class="tags light"><li>Downtown Richmond</li><li>Eastern Kentucky University area</li><li>Berea</li><li>Waco</li><li>Kirksville</li><li>Union City</li><li>Red House</li><li>Boonesborough</li></ul>
<h3>Weather history</h3><ol class="mini-tl"><li><b>1974</b><span>The April 3 Super Outbreak sent tornadoes across central Kentucky, including the counties around Richmond.</span></li><li><b>2008</b><span>Remnants of Hurricane Ike produced damaging wind across central Kentucky in mid-September.</span></li><li><b>2023</b><span>The March 3 windstorm downed trees and damaged roofs throughout the Bluegrass and beyond.</span></li></ol></section>
<h2>A County That Runs From Campus to Farmland</h2>
<p>Madison County packs a lot of property types into one place. Richmond’s core holds older homes and storefronts. The university area adds apartments, duplexes and rentals that change hands often. Then the land opens up into subdivisions, cattle farms and hillsides near the Kentucky River. Each brings its own claim pattern.</p>
<p>Hail and wind claims are the most frequent, and they tend to hit everything at once: roofs, gutters, siding, window screens and HVAC fins. The arguments come down to how much of each system is damaged and whether partial repair is realistic.</p>
<h2>Rental Property and Loss of Income</h2>
<p>Landlords near campus face a different set of issues. When a unit is unlivable after a storm or pipe break, lost rent may be part of the claim under a landlord or dwelling policy. Insurers sometimes shorten the repair period they will pay for, or price drywall and flooring as if one crew could finish in days. Real repair timelines, especially when several units are involved, often run longer.</p>
<ul>
<li>Document lease terms and monthly rents before the loss.</li>
<li>Track contractor scheduling delays in writing.</li>
<li>Note any code work required by the city before a unit can be reoccupied.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Roof Disputes Worth a Second Look</h2>
<p>Many Richmond-area claims involve a carrier that agrees there is hail damage but approves only a few squares of repair. Questions to ask: is the shingle line still made, can repaired sections blend, and were the steep-slope and two-story charges included? Our <a href="/insurance-appraisal/roof-hail-appraisal/">roof and hail appraisal</a> page covers the factors that usually decide these cases. If you just want to check the size of your roof against the estimate, the <a href="/appraisal-calculators/roof-measurement-calculator/">roof measurement calculator</a> is a good start.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Farm owners</b>Hay barns and equipment sheds may sit on a farm policy with separate limits. Confirm the limit before arguing about replacement cost.</div>
<h2>Our Approach in Madison County</h2>
<p>We do not work from photos alone. We inspect on site in Richmond, Berea and the surrounding countryside, then write an estimate that reflects what local contractors charge. If the carrier will not move, the appraisal clause lets each side name an appraiser and, if needed, an umpire. Most disputes narrow considerably once a detailed estimate is on the table.</p>
<p>Owners who are new to the process often ask whether they need a lawyer. Appraisal is designed to work without litigation, and many Madison County disputes are settled entirely between the two appraisers. Coverage questions, bad faith concerns or a denial of the whole claim are different matters, and for those an attorney is the right call.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services available in Richmond</h2><p>Every Kentucky Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Richmond and across Madison County, including:</p><ul><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/party-appraiser-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/home-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/roof-hail-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/tornado-wind-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal/fire-smoke-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Richmond claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can landlords near Eastern Kentucky University use appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p>Yes. Appraisal can resolve disputes over the cost of repairs and, depending on the policy, the amount of lost rental income.</p></details><details><summary>Do you inspect properties in Berea?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p>Yes. We cover Berea and all of Madison County, along with the rest of Kentucky.</p></details><details><summary>What if my insurer only approved a partial roof repair?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p>Partial approvals are a common appraisal issue. Matching, repairability and steep-slope charges often support a larger scope when documented properly.</p></details></div>
